    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1133">

                <pb facs="1118" n="1106" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg1106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 Pacific War/2257</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Swedish Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Boström</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Honorable the Minister of
                    Sweden in charge of Japanese interests in the Territory of Hawaii and refers to
                    a note dated December 31, 1942,<anchor n="86" xml:id="d1133-f1"/> setting <pb
                        facs="1119" n="1107" xml:id="pg1107"/> forth certain complaints of the
                    Japanese Government concerning the treatment alleged to have been accorded
                    Japanese civilians interned in the Territory of Hawaii.</p>
                <p>Investigation of these complaints has now been completed and there is transmitted
                    herewith a statement embodying the findings of the investigation. The paragraphs
                    of the enclosed statement are numbered to correspond with the numbered
                    paragraphs of the communication from the Japanese Government which formed the
                    enclosure to the Legation’s note under reference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-25">March 25,
                            1944</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1133-a1.xml" xpointer="d1133-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
